WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:03.780
<i>Hatsune Island.</i>

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:08.520
<i>The season of spring used to 
last forever on this island,</i>

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.760
<i>where there was one large 
cherry blossom tree.</i>

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.460
<i>A mysterious cherry blossom 
that would grant any wish.</i>

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.300
<i>The Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.</i>

00:00:21.150 --> 00:00:24.040
<i>This tree was a symbol 
of Hatsune Island,</i>

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:28.900
<i>and at some point it came 
to be known by that name.</i>

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>Hey, Nii-san...</i>

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>Nii-san...</i>

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:48.950
<i>Nii-san... Wake up...</i>

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.590
Come on, wake up!

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.010
Himeno?

00:00:58.490 --> 00:00:59.840
Umm...

00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.900
I'm in the Newspaper Club's room...?

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:06.180
Correct!

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.300
Did you sleep well,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:10.500
Yoshino Kiyotaka-kun?

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:17.590
You've got guts, falling asleep 
 while I'm in the middle of talking.

00:01:17.850 --> 00:01:20.190
I'm sorry, Ricca-san.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:21.590
Sheesh.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.500
Make sure you pay attention, okay?

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:26.000
I stayed up all night thinking about this.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:30.300
Now, now, Ricca. 
I think Taka-kun's learned his lesson.

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:31.950
Right?

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.670
And you, Charles,

00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:35.770
you were nodding off yourself, weren't you?

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:38.940
You could tell?

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:41.040
This is all because you two were

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.140
up late last night playing games together.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:44.880
I couldn't help it.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:48.100
The Lashian Plate rarely ever drops.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.090
Wait, how do you know that?

00:01:50.680 --> 00:01:52.420
The walls are thin in our apartments.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.390
You know that, Nii-san.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.930
You and Charles carry on too much late at night.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:00.370
But I've never heard you through them.

00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:06.090
Of course not! 
Unlike you, I'm not loud.

00:02:06.090 --> 00:02:11.910
Oh, but sometimes I feel like I'm 
hearing this oddly sexy voice...

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.760
I-I don't do that!

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:15.610
I don't do anything like that!

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.520
You don't do... what?

00:02:21.550 --> 00:02:22.750
Ahem.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:25.740
A-Anyway, be quiet at night.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:27.980
And don't eavesdrop on others!

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:29.190
All right.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.900
So, Sara.

00:02:30.900 --> 00:02:31.800
Yes?

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.630
While we're at it, could you 
wake up that other sleepyhead?

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.190
All right!

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:40.260
Aoi-chan, please wake up!

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.810
I-I can't.

00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.480
You can't?

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:47.240
Morizono-senpai is glaring at you.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.580
You need to wake up.

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:50.580
J-Just three more...

00:02:50.580 --> 00:02:51.680
Three more minutes?

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:53.020
Three more decades...

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.260
That long?!

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.620
Aoi-chan, if you don't wake up soon,

00:02:58.030 --> 00:02:59.520
you'll be late for work.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.430
R-Really?!

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.490
Wh-What time is it?!

00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:07.000
Change! I need to get changed quick!

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:12.040
Huh? Kiyotaka-san?

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:13.230
You guys, too?

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:16.610
Are you finally awake, 
Hinomoto Aoi-san?

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.120
Now then, once again.

00:03:24.540 --> 00:03:25.740
The meeting to decide what to

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:27.820
publish in the graduation edition
 of the official newspaper...

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:29.240
Begins now!

00:03:29.990 --> 00:03:33.490
<b>Cherry Blossoms Bloom</b>

00:03:35.890 --> 00:03:37.560
Newspaper Club

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.850
Now, take a look at the 
printouts I gave you earlier.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:40.300
Official Newspaper, Graduation Party Edition 
Main Theme: "Magic"

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.300
"Magic"?

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.030
I believe we should use magic 
as the theme for this issue!

00:03:45.970 --> 00:03:47.840
What's wrong, guys?

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:49.410
Yes, Ricca-san.

00:03:49.730 --> 00:03:50.640
Yes?

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:52.680
If "magic" is our theme,

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.060
what kind of articles are you planning to write?

00:03:55.060 --> 00:03:56.810
Isn't that obvious?

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.520
We're going to do a special 
report on a magic academy

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:02.820
that once existed in this world long ago!

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.360
It was in an academic city that existed 
in a vast, underground society,

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.890
where mages gathered from 
all around the world!

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.330
So, Ricca-san, I take it 
you were a student there?

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:14.230
Yes.

00:04:14.530 --> 00:04:20.240
They called me "The Lone Cattleya," 
and I was a category 5 mage.

00:04:16.530 --> 00:04:18.210
<b>"The Lone Cattleya"
*Image illustration</b>

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:22.040
Is that impressive?

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:23.210
Naturally.

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:28.230
After all, there were only five 
category 5 mages in the world.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:32.450
Though, it's not like rank 
represented a mage's entire value.

00:04:32.850 --> 00:04:35.050
That's quite the detailed story.

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:37.960
Don't call it a story! It's true!

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.950
U-Um...

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.930
I was active all across the world!

00:04:41.230 --> 00:04:43.260
Hey, Ricca.

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:45.930
Come back to the real world.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.100
I'm always living in the real world!

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:51.780
Why don't any of you understand?

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:52.770
How could we?

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:55.610
What?

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.680
You don't believe me either, Kiyotaka?

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.650
Are you saying you don't believe 
in the red string of fate

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:03.780
that's bound us since our previous lives?

00:05:05.320 --> 00:05:10.530
Well, putting aside whether 
or not I believe in it...

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.120
Kiyotaka! You're avoiding the question!

00:05:13.120 --> 00:05:15.060
Why magic?

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:17.280
Ricca-san?

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:19.230
Well...

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:22.730
It's to beat the unofficial newspaper!

00:05:23.520 --> 00:05:25.400
It pains me greatly to say this,

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.690
but right now,

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:29.240
the unofficial newspaper is beating us

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:29.910
<b>Unofficial</b>

00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.660
in fame,

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.680
Apr.    May    Jun.    Jul.    Aug.    Sep.    Oct.    Nov.    Dec.

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.680
<b>Unofficial</b>

00:05:29.910 --> 00:05:32.680
<b>Official</b>

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.680
and in the number of editions being published,

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:35.150
as I'm sure you're all aware.

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.810
That is true, but...

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:38.980
As president of the Newspaper Club,

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.150
I cannot allow this present state

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:44.050
to go on any longer!

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:48.490
But isn't that just Ricca's grudge

00:05:48.490 --> 00:05:51.960
against Suginami-kun from 
the unofficial newspaper?

00:05:51.960 --> 00:05:53.360
It's a personal grudge, right?

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.300
Yes, it's personal, isn't it?

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:56.830
I believe it's her grudge.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.370
It is, isn't it?

00:05:58.370 --> 00:06:00.100
You there, quiet!

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:07.310
That's why our next 
newspaper needs to prove

00:06:07.810 --> 00:06:10.210
to them which one is better.

00:06:10.210 --> 00:06:12.720
Then wouldn't it be better for us to go

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:14.290
with more traditional articles?

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.650
We are the official newspaper, after all.

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:17.690
Such as?

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.920
This edition is scheduled 
to be published before

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.130
the graduation ceremony, right?

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:23.490
So, how about a graduation special?

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:25.800
Yes, that sounds good.

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:28.730
We could do a special on the graduating classes,

00:06:28.730 --> 00:06:31.670
looking back on their memories 
of life here at school.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.740
Also, White Day comes right before it,

00:06:34.740 --> 00:06:36.970
so if we run a special on romance,

00:06:36.970 --> 00:06:39.080
I think girls will be interested in it.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.150
You're right. Girls love articles about romance.

00:06:43.150 --> 00:06:46.130
In that case, I think I could create a ranked list

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:49.940
of popular White Day items 
from the shopping district!

00:06:49.940 --> 00:06:50.950
How nice!

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:52.390
That sounds good.

00:06:52.390 --> 00:06:53.650
I think that's good.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.160
True...

00:06:57.350 --> 00:06:59.540
I'll admit that those are all wonderful ideas.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:01.170
However!

00:07:01.470 --> 00:07:02.570
They're too plain!

00:07:02.970 --> 00:07:05.400
We can't beat Suginami with those!

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:08.270
Therefore, I'll set them aside 
as our backup ideas.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:10.840
This is definitely personal.

00:07:10.840 --> 00:07:12.110
It's a grudge, isn't it?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.040
It's a grudge.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.680
She is childish.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:16.350
I said be quiet!

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.370
Who cares if it's personal?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:22.690
This time we have to get 
the better of Suginami!

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:25.130
But if magic is our theme,

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.430
what kind of articles are you planning to write?

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:29.560
Well, you see...

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.980
The Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree?

00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:37.140
You can't leave that out when you're

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:39.070
talking about magic on Hatsune Island.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:43.730
It's a magical cherry blossom tree 
that grants any wish, right?

00:07:43.730 --> 00:07:45.940
That's what the rumors say.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:48.210
But, long ago, the cherry blossoms

00:07:48.210 --> 00:07:50.880
really did bloom all year round, didn't they?

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:52.420
They did.

00:07:52.420 --> 00:07:54.260
Papa used to always tell me

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:56.990
stories about the cherry blossoms 
on Hatsune Island.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.860
I wonder why they went back to

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:00.660
being regular cherry blossom trees.

00:08:02.610 --> 00:08:05.180
Normally one would think 
something must have happened

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:07.980
on the day the cherry blossoms fell, but...

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:12.400
Yes, that's right!

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:17.840
Long ago, the cherry blossoms 
were in bloom all year long.

00:08:17.840 --> 00:08:22.560
However, one day, they all became 
regular cherry blossoms.

00:08:23.110 --> 00:08:26.070
Why would the Everlasting Cherry Blossom 
Tree suddenly become a normal one?

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.810
How did it come to be known as a magical

00:08:29.810 --> 00:08:32.490
cherry blossom tree 
that would grant any wish?

00:08:35.440 --> 00:08:36.880
Nobody knows.

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:39.910
If anyone does know, 
they refuse to come forward.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.430
So everything remains a mystery...

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.600
Don't you find that a bit strange?

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.470
Now that you mention it, yes.

00:08:47.230 --> 00:08:49.970
I don't really get it, though, 
since it's been a normal

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:53.040
cherry blossom tree ever since I was born.

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:57.850
I only listened to the stories as fairy tales, too.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.950
But the cherry blossoms 
on Hatsune Island really

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:02.600
were in bloom all year long.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.790
My Papa was actually alive 
during those times.

00:09:06.790 --> 00:09:08.960
That's why I believe

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.630
that it was magic.

00:09:12.270 --> 00:09:13.450
Magic...

00:09:20.210 --> 00:09:21.880
It's been a while since I last came here.

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:22.920
Me, too.

00:09:22.920 --> 00:09:25.810
Since we're here, why don't we test it?

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:27.480
"Test"? Test what?

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:29.550
The rumors you mentioned

00:09:29.550 --> 00:09:31.150
about the Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.650
The one about it granting any wish?

00:09:33.650 --> 00:09:36.370
Yes. If something does 
happen, then why don't

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.160
we make that the main article 
for our next newspaper?

00:09:39.620 --> 00:09:41.560
I think that might be interesting.

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:45.780
Any wish, huh...?

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.070
You too, Kiyotaka.

00:09:48.340 --> 00:09:49.280
All right.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:56.210
What are you all wishing for?

00:09:56.410 --> 00:09:57.380
It's a secret.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.580
Mine's a secret from you too, Taka-kun.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.450
I can't tell you, Nii-san.

00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:04.450
I-It's nothing to do with you, Senpai!

00:10:04.850 --> 00:10:08.500
Oh, everyone seems so serious about this.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:10.390
I won't fall behind, either!

00:10:10.900 --> 00:10:13.160
And what are you going 
to wish for, Kiyotaka?

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.770
Well, I don't have any 
particular wish in mind...

00:10:22.810 --> 00:10:24.300
<i>A wish, huh...</i>

00:10:25.400 --> 00:10:28.460
Everyone, leave your hand on 
the tree and close your eyes,

00:10:28.460 --> 00:10:30.720
then try making the wish in your mind.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:33.140
Don't think that it won't be granted,

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:35.310
or that magic doesn't exist,

00:10:35.770 --> 00:10:40.860
or anything like that, 
and wish from your heart.

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:46.840
<i>May I continue to enjoy a pleasant life</i>

00:10:46.840 --> 00:10:49.150
<i>with these club members...</i>

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:54.310
<i>Forever, just as we are now.</i>

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:05.190
What's gotten into you 
all of a sudden, Kiyotaka?

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:07.520
We were just focusing and...

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:12.180
Th-The cherry blossoms...

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:36.470
The cherry blossoms are blooming...?

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:39.960
Wh-What happened here?

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:42.560
The tree is in full bloom...

00:11:42.560 --> 00:11:46.020
W-W-We're not dreaming, are we?

00:11:46.650 --> 00:11:50.410
The everlasting cherry blossom 
tree... has revived?

00:11:50.410 --> 00:11:52.220
Is it because of our wishes?

00:11:52.410 --> 00:11:57.260
Maybe it bloomed again in 
order to grant our wishes?

00:11:57.490 --> 00:11:58.770
I see.

00:11:58.770 --> 00:12:01.170
It's very pretty when you put it that way.

00:12:01.300 --> 00:12:03.500
It's very romantic!

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:06.000
I-Incredible. It's incredible!

00:12:06.260 --> 00:12:09.070
See?! I told you magic exists!

00:12:09.360 --> 00:12:10.740
<i>You received a text message.</i>

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:12.140
I've got a text.

00:12:12.390 --> 00:12:14.160
Oh, I have one, too.

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:15.350
Me, too.

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:16.910
Is it from Mom?

00:12:16.910 --> 00:12:19.080
Maybe mine's from someone at work.

00:12:19.440 --> 00:12:21.320
The cherry blossoms just 
bloomed all of a sudden,

00:12:21.320 --> 00:12:23.300
so I imagine everyone on Hatsune Island

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.220
is texting or calling someone right now.

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:27.420
What's this?

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:30.190
"When the cherry blossoms bloom,

00:12:30.190 --> 00:12:32.200
go the promised place, and..."

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.200
Huh?

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:35.390
Oh, sorry.

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:37.640
I thought someone texted me by mistake,

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:39.820
but it sounds a bit ominous.

00:12:40.280 --> 00:12:42.340
Ricca, you got the same message, too?

00:12:42.340 --> 00:12:45.300
Huh? You mean you got this, too?

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:47.610
I got the same message, too.

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:51.020
Me, too. The sender's unknown, though...

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:52.380
Meaning...

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.310
Yeah.

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:57.550
Everyone here got the same message?

00:12:57.550 --> 00:12:58.990
It seems so.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.430
Here, look at this.

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:06.700
The time sent says April 30th, 1951!

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:08.900
Wow, you're right!

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:11.400
1951...

00:13:11.630 --> 00:13:14.470
Meaning this is a message from the past?

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:16.430
And over a century ago, too?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:22.300
I wonder if the sender messed 
up their date settings,

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:24.000
or if the data got corrupted.

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:28.300
Part of the text is garbled, so maybe it did.

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:31.470
That's the natural way to think about it.

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:33.920
You can't send messages from the past.

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:36.970
No, that's not it!

00:13:36.970 --> 00:13:38.470
Why not?

00:13:38.470 --> 00:13:41.760
Because it'd be boring if it were!

00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:43.910
Everything is all connected!

00:13:45.190 --> 00:13:46.200
True...

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.930
So I'm sure that this date must also be

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:53.840
a part of the message 
someone has sent us

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.220
from that moment over a century ago!

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:00.150
"When the cherry blossoms bloom, 
go to the promised place, and..."

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.560
And, just now, the cherry 
blossoms have bloomed!

00:14:04.220 --> 00:14:05.990
Where is the "promised place"?

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:08.280
What is going to happen there?

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:12.080
And why have the cherry 
blossoms bloomed now?

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:15.250
I think we've settled on the 
theme for our next newspaper,

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:16.300
haven't we?

00:14:30.450 --> 00:14:32.280
Taka-kun, Taka-kun.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:34.710
Are you going to sleep already?

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:36.990
No, not yet.

00:14:36.990 --> 00:14:39.990
Then, can we talk for a bit?

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:41.200
Yeah, sure.

00:14:45.860 --> 00:14:48.710
Well, it's kind of cold, isn't it?

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:52.450
Then shouldn't you be getting 
to bed soon, Lulu-nee?

00:14:55.800 --> 00:14:57.980
Why are you giving me that look?

00:14:57.980 --> 00:14:59.340
Because!

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:02.060
Think about it one more time.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:06.840
I told you, "It's kind of cold, isn't it?"

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.920
Now, how do you answer?

00:15:09.270 --> 00:15:12.100
If you want, I can pull out 
another blanket for you?

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.070
U-Umm...

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:18.300
If you can't figure it out, then fine!

00:15:21.730 --> 00:15:23.840
Now, next topic.

00:15:23.840 --> 00:15:26.470
It was really surprising to see the 
cherry blossoms bloom, wasn't it?

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:29.850
Yeah, it felt like a dream.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.230
Do you think they

00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:34.510
actually bloomed in order 
to grant our wishes?

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.610
Who knows?

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.980
I do think that's a 
romantic idea, though.

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:44.480
If the cherry blossoms really did 
bloom to grant our wishes, then...

00:15:44.480 --> 00:15:45.450
Wait,

00:15:46.900 --> 00:15:49.790
it really doesn't make sense!

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:51.600
What doesn't make sense?

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:55.860
All right! I'm done beating around the bush.

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:58.850
It's not like you'd pick 
up on the hint anyway!

00:16:00.230 --> 00:16:01.210
Taka-kun.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.610
Let's sleep together tonight!

00:16:05.620 --> 00:16:06.380
Huh?

00:16:06.690 --> 00:16:10.320
I said, let's sleep together tonight!

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:13.320
No, that's a little too...

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:14.640
You don't want to?

00:16:14.640 --> 00:16:16.750
But you used to sleep with me before...

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.140
That was back when you were still a kid,

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.870
and you said you were scared because

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:23.730
you came to Japan all by yourself...

00:16:23.730 --> 00:16:25.460
Pardon me.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.950
H-Hey, Lulu-nee!

00:16:31.880 --> 00:16:36.210
Yay! It's been so long since 
we slept together, Taka-kun.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.880
Taka-kun!

00:16:38.430 --> 00:16:40.180
Look, Lulu-nee!

00:16:40.410 --> 00:16:41.660
What?

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:46.600
L-Lulu-nee, I think you 
need to be more aware

00:16:46.600 --> 00:16:49.470
of the fact that you're 
an attractive... woman.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:53.020
Okay!

00:16:53.290 --> 00:16:56.360
Jeez, you're not aware 
of it all, are you?!

00:16:56.790 --> 00:16:57.800
You're wrong.

00:16:57.800 --> 00:17:00.370
I'm doing this because I'm aware.

00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:03.640
Good night, Taka-kun.

00:17:18.330 --> 00:17:22.040
Good grief, she really 
did sleep with me...

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:25.530
Taka-kun,
 I have work to do
 for the student council,
 so I'm going on ahead.
 Charles

00:17:23.610 --> 00:17:26.420
<i>All of Hatsune Island is 
talking about their shock</i>

00:17:25.880 --> 00:17:27.580
Must be rough every day.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.740
<i>and surprise at seeing 
the cherry blossoms bloom</i>

00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:30.660
<i>again after 20 years.</i>

00:17:30.930 --> 00:17:35.170
<b>The Everlasting Cherry Blossom
revived!!</b>

00:17:31.260 --> 00:17:33.050
<i>Here at Sakura Park, people have been</i>

00:17:33.050 --> 00:17:35.430
<i>coming since morning to see 
the cherry blossoms and—</i>

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:38.950
<i>The Tourist Association is 
running with the catchphrase,</i>

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.630
I guess it wasn't just a dream?

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:41.640
<i>"Come see the Everlasting Cherry 
Blossom Tree revived," and...</i>

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:43.670
Nii-san.

00:17:45.800 --> 00:17:46.680
Good morning.

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:48.620
Yeah, good morning.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:52.110
It's cold again this morning.

00:17:52.110 --> 00:17:53.440
Yeah, it is.

00:17:53.440 --> 00:17:55.820
It really looks like it's spring, though.

00:17:56.140 --> 00:17:59.450
Good morning, Senpai. Katsuragi-san.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:01.000
Good morning!

00:18:01.300 --> 00:18:04.480
Good morning, Rukawa-san. Hinomoto-san.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.460
I heard the Everlasting Cherry 
Blossom bloomed again.

00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:12.130
It's become quite the stir, hasn't it?

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.130
It's been 20 years.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.810
Well, of course.

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:14.740
The rumors were true.

00:18:13.810 --> 00:18:16.240
The cherry blossoms are 
blooming again after 20 years.

00:18:14.740 --> 00:18:16.240
Incredible.

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:20.040
Everyone's feeling the mystique of 
the Everlasting Cherry Blossom Tree.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:25.610
I'm not Ricca, but it does 
feel like magic or fate.

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:27.440
It really is mysterious.

00:18:27.930 --> 00:18:31.780
Let's start investigating 
those mysteries one by one.

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:42.980
Well, well, if it isn't all the 
members of the Newspaper Club.

00:18:43.590 --> 00:18:46.110
Do you need something, Suginami-senpai?

00:18:46.510 --> 00:18:50.300
I figured I'd come give you guys 
a little declaration of war.

00:18:50.300 --> 00:18:51.830
Declaration of war?

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:54.560
I'm planning to have the 
next unofficial newspaper

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:57.900
feature articles unraveling the 
mystery of the Everlasting

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.650
Cherry Blossom Tree that 
started blooming yesterday.

00:19:01.130 --> 00:19:04.030
And you all call yourselves 
the Newspaper Club.

00:19:04.030 --> 00:19:07.410
Of course, you're planning to 
unravel this mystery as well, yes?

00:19:07.410 --> 00:19:08.530
Naturally.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:13.060
So, I thought we should make 
a competition out of it.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:15.200
A competition over what?

00:19:15.490 --> 00:19:19.080
A competition to see who can 
delve deeper into this mystery,

00:19:19.080 --> 00:19:22.140
and write the most interesting 
article about it.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.740
And I'm sure you're planning 
to say the loser has

00:19:24.740 --> 00:19:27.450
to accept the winner's 
demand or something, right?

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:28.550
Isn't that obvious?

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.850
Sorry, but we refuse.

00:19:31.060 --> 00:19:33.380
Now, now, why don't we take them on?

00:19:33.380 --> 00:19:34.050
Huh?

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:36.950
They're inviting us, after all.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.100
But, Ricca-san...

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:44.470
I expect no less of my 
rival, Morizono Ricca.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:45.400
You're quick to understand.

00:19:45.840 --> 00:19:49.520
So, I'll tell you what 
our demand is if we win.

00:19:49.890 --> 00:19:51.200
Very well, let's hear it.

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:54.000
If our Newspaper Club wins,

00:19:54.000 --> 00:19:56.170
I want you to quit publishing 
the unofficial newspaper

00:19:56.170 --> 00:19:58.790
for as long as you attend this school.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:00.110
Oh?

00:20:00.460 --> 00:20:02.830
You wish to stop the unofficial newspaper

00:20:02.830 --> 00:20:05.240
that's been published for over 50 years?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.690
How dare you insult Suginami-sama so?!

00:20:07.990 --> 00:20:10.070
Mikoto-san, good morning!

00:20:10.410 --> 00:20:12.830
Yes, good morning, Hinomoto Aoi.

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:15.880
Wait, why are you casually 
greeting me right now?!

00:20:16.290 --> 00:20:18.270
That is our demand.

00:20:18.270 --> 00:20:19.690
Don't ignore me!

00:20:19.950 --> 00:20:23.390
Interesting. We'll accept 
your demand, then.

00:20:23.660 --> 00:20:24.880
Suginami-sama!

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:26.560
So, Suginami.

00:20:27.050 --> 00:20:28.460
What's your demand?

00:20:30.490 --> 00:20:31.910
Our demand is...

00:20:32.510 --> 00:20:34.740
Yoshino Kiyotaka! It's you.

00:20:36.370 --> 00:20:38.470
I want you!

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:40.900
Whaaaa?!

00:20:41.730 --> 00:20:45.060
If we win, I'll be taking

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.820
Yoshino Kiyotaka as my personal partner!

00:20:48.170 --> 00:20:51.390
Hold on a minute! Why me?

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:52.600
Yoshino,

00:20:52.960 --> 00:20:55.730
I want you!

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:57.900
H-Hey...

00:20:57.900 --> 00:20:59.060
All right.

00:20:59.770 --> 00:21:01.460
Then those are the conditions 
for our competition.

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:02.480
Whaaa?!

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:06.060
You don't need to worry, Kiyotaka.

00:21:06.300 --> 00:21:08.600
Do you have some kind of plan to win?

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:09.660
Yes.

00:21:10.390 --> 00:21:12.270
There's no way someone like Suginami

00:21:12.270 --> 00:21:16.100
can break the red string of fate that's

00:21:16.100 --> 00:21:18.670
bound you and me together 
for over a century, right?

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:21.620
Ah, well, but...

00:21:22.020 --> 00:21:23.790
Now I'm even more motivated!

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:27.180
The Graduation Party Edition of the 
Official Newspaper, a special on magic!

00:21:27.490 --> 00:21:29.200
Everyone, let's give it our all!

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:30.970
Yeah!

00:23:25.100 --> 00:23:40.380
<b>A Warm Place</b>

00:23:26.090 --> 00:23:28.140
I can't believe the Everlasting 
Cherry Blossom Tree's blooming again.

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:28.850
Is it magic?

00:23:28.850 --> 00:23:30.720
Taka-kun! Let's sleep together!

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:31.460
Lulu-nee!

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:34.080
Come on, you're my only cousin.

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:35.280
Hey, hold on!

00:23:35.280 --> 00:23:37.120
Next time: A Warm Place

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:39.880
Taka-kun, rely on me more.
